   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to providing for the\nfinancing and construction of facilities for Village of Lake Placid, Inc.",
    "basePrintNo": "S9005",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9005-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1676 & 1680, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S9005\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to providing for the financing and construction of facilities\nfor Village of Lake Placid, Inc.\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis designates the Village of Lake Placid, Inc. as a \"dormitory\" and\n\"educational institution\" for purposes of the Dormitory Authority Act.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds the Village of Lake Placid, Inc. to paragraph (b) of\nsubdivision 2 of section 1676 of the Public Authorities Law.\n\nSection 2 adds the Village of Lake Placid, Inc. to subdivision 1 of\nsection 1680 of the Public Authorities Law.\n\nSection 3 adds a new paragraph 1 granting the power and authority to the\nVillage of Lake Placid, Inc. to enter into a lease, sublease or other\nagreement with the Dormitory Authority.\n\nSection 4 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPresently, under state law, municipalities are eligible for financing\nand construction of facilities from the New York State Dormitory Author-\nity. The main purpose behind this partnership with DASNY and the Village\nof Lake Placid is to design, construct and finance a much-needed parking\ngarage in the center of Lake Placid.\n\nThe Village will be undertaking a major road reconstruction project next\nyear through downtown Lake Placid. The project involves new storm sewers\nthat will redirect storm water away from Mirror Lake.  The Village will\nalso replace/upgrade waterlines to meet the growing demand and replace\nold infrastructure.\n\nTo improve traffic flow and widen traffic lanes for cyclists, the\nVillage will be removing a parking lane from one side of the road in\nvarious sections. With the loss of this parking lane, the Village needs\nto address ways to provide adequate parking. In order to accommodate the\nmany venues being held in the Village such as the upcoming World Univer-\nsity games and other international events the Village wants to move\nforward with the construction of a parking garage.\n\nLake Placid is one of the largest generators of sales tax in Essex Coun-\nty. A parking garage will improve foot traffic into local retail estab-\nlishments while alleviating the on street-parking burden. This legis-\nlation is required to allow the village of Lake Placid to move forward\nwith a proposed parking garage through a partnership with DASNY.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
